  "name": "Question 16",
  "problem": "Find the $25$th percentile of the random variable $X$ if the probability distribution function of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2}-1,\\, & 2<x<4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The $100p$th percentile of a random variable $X$ is the number ${x}_{p}$ such that\n\n$$\nP(X\\le {x}_{p})=p.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we want to find the $25$th percentile, which corresponds to the decimal $p=0.25.$ We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le {x}_{0.25}) & ={\\int }_{2}^{{x}_{0.25}}(\\frac{x}{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-x)|}_{2}^{{x}_{0.25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.25}^{2}}{4}-{x}_{0.25}-(\\frac{(2)^{2}}{4}-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}_{0.25}^{2}}{4}-{x}_{0.25}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $25$th percentile is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}_{0.25}^{2}}{4}-{x}_{0.25}+1 & =0.25 \\\\ {x}_{0.25}^{2}-4{x}_{0.25}+3 & =0 \\\\ ({x}_{0.25}-3)({x}_{0.25}-1) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{0.25}=1,\\,3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we take the root ${x}_{0.25}=3$ because $2<{x}_{0.25}<4.$",
